 Committee","date":"12/08/2026","key":true},{"title":"Full Council - 202526 Revenue Capital and Treasury Outturn","url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk/documents/s25829/full-council-202526-revenue-capital-and-treasury-outturn.pdf","committee":"Full Council","date":"28/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Appendix 1 - Executive 16 July 26 Outturn Report","url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk/documents/s25820/appendix-1-executive-16-july-26-outturn-report.pdf","committee":"Full Council","date":"28/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Appendix 2 - Capital Programme 2025-26 to 2028-29","url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk/documents/s25821/appendix-2-capital-programme-2025-26-to-2028-29.pdf","committee":"Full Council","date":"28/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"2026-07-15 final report Full Council, Enhancement of Local Nature Reserves using DCC s106 funding","url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk/documents/s25823/2026-07-15-final-report-full-council-enhancement-of-local-na.pdf","committee":"Full Council","date":"28/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Strata Budget Monitoring Outturn 2025-26","url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk/documents/s25805/strata-budget-monitoring-outturn-2025-26.pdf","committee":"Strata - Joint Executive Committee","date":"22/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Appendix A Budget Monitoring (2) May 2025-26","url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk/documents/s25806/appendix-a-budget-monitoring-2-may-2025-26.pdf","committee":"Strata - Joint Executive Committee","date":"22/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Strata Budget Monitoring Outturn 2025-26","url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk/documents/s25807/strata-budget-monitoring-outturn-2025-26.pdf","committee":"Strata - Joint Executive Committee","date":"22/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Appendix A Budget Monitoring Outturn 2025-26","url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk/documents/s25808/appendix-a-budget-monitoring-outturn-2025-26.pdf","committee":"Strata - Joint Executive Committee","date":"22/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Report Executive 16 July 26 Outturn Report","url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk/documents/s25767/report-executive-16-july-26-outturn-report.pdf","committee":"Executive","date":"16/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Appendix 1 - Capital Programme 2025-26 to 2028-29","url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk/documents/s25768/appendix-1-capital-programme-2025-26-to-2028-29.pdf","committee":"Executive","date":"16/07/2026","key":true}],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-29","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-01","committee":"Governance Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-06","committee":"Executive","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-03","committee":"Executive","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-05","committee":"Full Council","time":"10.00 am","status":"Moved","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-28","committee":"Full Council","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-08-11","committee":"Executive","time":"10.00 am","status":"Cancelled","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-08-12","committee":"Strata - Joint Scrutiny Committee","time":"2.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Executive","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Wolborough planning appeal generating \u00a30.075m legal cost overspend with unresolved exposure","lead":"Litigation costs represent contingent liability exposure; appeals can extend beyond a single financial year and create uncertain budget impact.","iso":"2026-09-15","paper_title":"Report Q1 Monitoring 2627","paper_url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk/documents/s25969/25969.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Storm damage costs materializing in Q1: \u00a30.098m drawn from Coastal Resilience Reserve in first quarter following severe weather","lead":"Coastal and weather-related damage costs are materializing faster than planned, depleting a reserve set aside for resilience and indicating ongoing environmental risk that could require further spending.","iso":"2026-09-15","paper_title":"Report Q1 Monitoring 2627","paper_url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk/documents/s25969/25969.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Major capital projects forecast to slip: Sherborne House \u00a36.2m and Waste Transfer Station \u00a33.3m commitments will not be fully incurred in-year","lead":"Capital project execution risk indicates the council may not deliver its capital programme on schedule, affecting asset delivery and creating refinancing exposure if cash needs to be borrowed.","iso":"2026-09-15","paper_title":"Report Q1 Monitoring 2627","paper_url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk/documents/s25969/25969.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Report Q1 Monitoring 2627","paper_url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk/documents/s25969/25969.pdf","headline":"Wolborough planning appeal generating \u00a30.075m legal cost overspend with unresolved exposure","detail":"Development Management is forecasting a \u00a30.075m overspend on legal fees that is 'largely associated with the Wolborough appeal.' This represents ongoing litigation on a significant planning matter with cost exposure that may extend beyond the current financial year.","category":"other","matters":"Litigation costs represent contingent liability exposure; appeals can extend beyond a single financial year and create uncertain budget impact.","figures":"\u00a30.075m forecast legal overspend, Development Management service","quote":"This position is partly offset by a forecast \u00a30.075m overspend on legal fees, largely associated with the Wolborough appeal.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Report Q1 Monitoring 2627","paper_url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk/documents/s25969/25969.pdf","headline":"Storm damage costs materializing in Q1: \u00a30.098m drawn from Coastal Resilience Reserve in first quarter following severe weather","detail":"The council has already spent \u00a30.098m from its Coastal Resilience Reserve in Q1 for emergency repairs: Teignmouth Promenade (\u00a30.049m) and Great Cliff Works (\u00a30.049m) following damage from Storm Ingrid. The opening reserve balance was \u00a30.250m; forecast closing is \u00a30.152m. The report explicitly flags that 'there will have to be close observation of the pressures on the Coastal Resilience Reserve as the long hot summer continues.'","category":"demand","matters":"Coastal and weather-related damage costs are materializing faster than planned, depleting a reserve set aside for resilience and indicating ongoing environmental risk that could require further spending.","figures":"\u00a30.098m drawn in Q1 (Promenade \u00a30.049m + Cliffs \u00a30.049m); reserve declining from \u00a30.250m opening to \u00a30.152m forecast closing","quote":"In particular, there will have to be close observation of the pressures on the Coastal Resilience Reserve as the long hot summer continues.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Report Q1 Monitoring 2627","paper_url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk/documents/s25969/25969.pdf","headline":"Major capital projects forecast to slip: Sherborne House \u00a36.2m and Waste Transfer Station \u00a33.3m commitments will not be fully incurred in-year","detail":"Of the reprofiled \u00a333.6m capital budget, only \u00a32.8m (8.4%) has been spent by end of Q1. A further \u00a313.8m is committed but not yet incurred, with significant multiyear projects \u2014 Sherborne House (\u00a36.2m) and Waste Transfer Station (\u00a33.3m) \u2014 expected to slip from prior years into future years. The forecast outturn reflects 'expected slippage on the Sherborne House and Waste Transfer Station projects from prior years not being fully caught up in-year.'","category":"capital","matters":"Capital project execution risk indicates the council may not deliver its capital programme on schedule, affecting asset delivery and creating refinancing exposure if cash needs to be borrowed.","figures":"\u00a32.8m spent of \u00a333.6m reprofiled budget (8.4%); \u00a36.2m Sherborne House, \u00a33.3m WTS committed but slipping","quote":"A significant proportion of these commitments relate to multiyear projects, including \u00a36.2m for Sherborne House and \u00a33.3m for the Waste Transfer Station, and will not necessarily be incurred during 2026/27.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Report Q1 Monitoring 2627","paper_url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk/documents/s25969/25969.pdf","headline":"Food waste grant of \u00a30.195m expected in budget is no longer forecast to be received","detail":"The Waste, Recycling & Cleansing service is reporting a \u00a30.111m overspend, largely because an expected food waste grant of \u00a30.195m that was included in the approved budget is now not expected to arrive. The shortfall is only partly offset by additional Extended Producer Responsibility grant income (\u00a30.050m) and underspend on workshop parts.","category":"income","matters":"An expected funding stream materializing later or not at all represents unexpected income volatility and removes a contingency the council planned to rely on.","figures":"\u00a30.195m grant loss, Waste service \u00a30.111m overspend forecast","quote":"largely because a \u00a30.195m food waste grant included in the budget is no longer expected to be received","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Review of Council Tax premiums and discount changes for ONS 15.9.26","paper_url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk/documents/s25958/25958.pdf","headline":"No Valuation Tribunal appeals or material legal challenges to any policy change despite significant charge increases","detail":"Despite implementing substantial Council Tax increases (up to 100% premium charges), the Council has not received any Tribunal appeals regarding the second homes premium. Initial customer complaints diminished after explanation and mitigation options were offered. For the major repairs discount removal, the Council noted that historical challenges were often from landlords disagreeing with the 'uninhabitable' assessment criteria, not the principle.","category":"governance","matters":"Absence of legal challenge to significant revenue-raising changes demonstrates the policies are defensible and that the Council executed them competently with proper notice, communication, and exception processes.","figures":"Zero Tribunal appeals received; 535 exceptions processed with clear criteria; customer contact diminished after initial period","quote":"To date, despite the significant uplift in council tax, we have not received any Tribunal appeals about the 100% Premiums for unoccupied and substantially furnished properties.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-15"},"name":"Teignbridge","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-20","since_iso":"2026-08-21","distress":false,"headline":"Wolborough planning appeal generating \u00a30.075m legal cost overspend with unresolved exposure","lead":"Litigation costs represent contingent liability exposure; appeals can extend beyond a single financial year and create uncertain budget impact.","also":["15 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Audit Committee on 2026-09-29","n_findings":16,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Report Q1 Monitoring 2627","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.teignbridge.gov.uk/documents/s25969/25969.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":85,"news_drafts_total":3}}